# Line endings.
#
# The team is split across macOS and Windows. Without this, Windows checkouts
# get CRLF, which produces two failures that are hard to attribute:
#
#   · a shell script or SQL file with CRLF fails inside the Linux container
#     with an error that never mentions line endings
#   · every file looks entirely rewritten in a diff, so review is impossible
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository while letting Windows check
# out CRLF where that is harmless. The explicit `eol=lf` entries are files that
# are executed by Linux and must be LF on disk everywhere.

* text=auto

# Executed by Linux — must be LF on disk, on every platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# Source and docs: normalise in the repository.
*.py            text
*.md            text
*.toml          text
*.js            text
*.html          text
*.css           text
*.json          text

# Binary — never touch these.
*.docx          binary
*.pdf           binary
*.pptx          binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
